  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to run",
      "items": [
        "cd rust && cargo run --release --bin ed -- [--lmin 4] [--lmax 6] [--gamma 0.01] [--seed 1] [--open 0|1]  (needs MKL: $MKL_LIB_DIR or ~/anaconda3/lib)",
        "cargo run --release --bin entanglement -- [--L 12 | --lmin 8 --lmax 12] [--seed 1]  (L ≤ 14)",
        "cargo run --release --bin lindblad_entanglement -- [--gamma 0.01 | --gamma 0] [--L 6 | --lmin 4 --lmax 6] [--seed 1]  (L = 7: 18 min, 4.4 GB)",
        "The binaries write to data/ (or $SCARS_DATA_DIR); the current CSVs sit in data/used_data/",
        "Then plot_entanglement.py, plot_operator_entanglement.py, plot_lindblad_entanglement.py [dir] (default data/used_data); plot_spectrum.py reads data/",
        "Figures are copied by hand to latex/figures/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Notes part",
      "items": [
        "Compile: latex/build_parts.sh spectra → latex/parts/pdf/spectra.pdf (full notes are built first; numbering as in latex/notes.tex)",
        "Figures used (copied to latex/figures/): entanglement.png, operator_entanglement.png, lindblad_entanglement_g0.01.png",
        "1 Model",
        "2 Theory: 2.2 Scars, thermalization and entanglement",
        "3 How the simulations are done: Notation, Pauli strings, Density matrices (Pauli basis), Spectra and eigenstates, Entanglement entropy, Operator entanglement, Eigenvalues without LAPACK",
        "11 Entanglement of eigenstates and Liouvillian modes",
        "spectrum.png belongs to the appendix of earlier results (previous coefficients), not to this part"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Key mechanics",
      "items": [
        "LAPACK comes from Intel MKL (libmkl_rt), linked only into these three binaries by rust/build.rs ($MKL_LIB_DIR or ~/anaconda3/lib)",
        "Every binary builds H with Params::random_c and Rng(1000 · seed + L): the same realization as all other runs",
        "ed: γ = 0 diagonalizes H (zheevd) and uses the modes |m⟩⟨n|; γ > 0 runs dgeev on the dense real 4^L × 4^L 𝓛, then tower / mixed / bulk weights of each right eigenvector",
        "lindblad_entanglement: degenerate eigenspaces are re-diagonalized with zhegv in the energy form; S_op of ρ_L = XX†/Tr and ρ_R = X†X/Tr from zheevd",
        "entanglement: one small zheevd of ρ_A per eigenstate; scars = tower weight > 1/2",
        "plot_clik.py also reads lindblad_entanglement_L<L>_g<γ>.csv and spectrum_open_L<L>.csv as the ED reference for CLIK"
      ]
    }
  ]
